  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dairy Microenterprise, Business and Gender in Irpa Chico, Phase II, Municipality of Viachan, Bolivia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asociacion de Mujeres Aymaras Lecheras de Irpa Chico (AMALIC) will increase its membership to approximately 100 dairy farmers, mostly Aymara women, from six communities in the municipality of Viacha on the Bolivian altiplano. It will finish construction of a new plant, meeting national food safety regulations, to increase the current output of its dairy enterprise and develop new value-added products that will meet the demands of local and regional markets, including school breakfast and lunch programs. Expected results include improved organizational, administrative, production and marketing capacity for AMALIC and a higher income for its membership.</narrative>
  </description>
